# ============================================================================
# LibreRun — the LLM gateway's own environment
# Copy to gateway.env and fill in values:  cp gateway.env.example gateway.env
# Then make it owner-only:                 chmod 600 gateway.env
# Never commit gateway.env (.gitignore already excludes it).
#
# Read by ONE process: the `gateway` service, which loads this file as a
# second env_file beside the derived agent-keys.env (compose.yaml). The
# backend never receives it and never reads it — a provider credential in
# the backend is a credential every in-process agent shares (decisions
# L23, L28). That is the whole reason this file exists separately from
# the root .env, which is read by compose, by the backend and by the
# frontend build.
#
# The file is OPTIONAL. Without it the gateway starts with no provider
# credential, which is exactly what the keyless demo wants
# (LIBRERUN_STUB_LLM=true answers every step from fixtures). The demo
# writes one anyway, holding nothing but the gateway's store key below,
# so a provider key pasted in Admin -> Settings has somewhere to be kept
# (K7); `librerun demo` and ./scripts/demo.sh make it owner-only.
#
# Which provider and model serve each step is NOT configured here: it
# comes from the agent's manifest (llm.steps) and the admin
# agent-configuration page, per tenant. Set a key below for every
# provider those choices reference.
#
# See docs/authoring/LLM_Gateway.md §3 for the two credentials — these
# provider keys, which are the gateway's, and the per-agent gateway keys
# (LIBRERUN_AGENT_KEY_<ID>), which stay in the root .env.
#
# Secrets as files (decision L30): each key below can come from a FILE
# instead — set <NAME>_FILE to a path and leave <NAME> blank, and the
# gateway reads the file, stripping one trailing newline. That is how
# Docker, Podman and Kubernetes secrets reach this process with no
# wrapper, and it keeps the value out of `docker inspect`. Setting both
# to different values stops the gateway by name rather than picking one.
# docs/platform/Install.md, "Secrets as files", has the compose overlay.
#
# THE CLASSES (K4, decision L29): every variable in the deployment sits
# in exactly one class and in exactly one example file;
# `.env.example`'s header explains the four. This file carries three.
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# [1] BOOTSTRAP — must be in the environment
# ============================================================================
# ---- The gateway's store key (K7; decisions L33, D33) ----
#
# The key the gateway's own rows in the secrets store are sealed with: the
# provider keys pasted in Admin -> Settings, and the keypair the browser
# seals them to. A comma-separated list of Fernet keys, the first one
# current — the shape of the backend's LIBRERUN_BACKEND_SECRETS_KEY, and
# NEVER the same key: the gateway refuses to start when its key also
# sealed a backend row. Generate one:
#   head -c 32 /dev/urandom | base64 | tr '+/' '-_'
# Blank means unconfigured: this file's provider keys serve alone, and the
# admin page says a key cannot be pasted here. Here or as a _FILE, never in
# compose's `environment:` block, where a blank would override this file.
# docs/platform/Install.md, "The gateway's store key", has rotation.
LIBRERUN_GATEWAY_SECRETS_KEY=
# or LIBRERUN_GATEWAY_SECRETS_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/gateway_secrets_key

# ============================================================================
# [4] SECRETS — where each one lives
# ============================================================================
# ---- Provider credentials (this process and no other) ----
#
# One line per provider your steps name; leave the rest blank. No inline
# comments here on purpose: this is the file a key gets pasted into, and
# `NAME=sk-... # note` is a value with a note in it under some parsers.
#
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# or OPENAI_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/openai_api_key
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/anthropic_api_key
# https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY=
# or GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/google_ai_api_key

# ============================================================================
# [2] POSTURE — in the environment by policy
# ============================================================================
# ---- What one knowledge-base search may spend ----
#
# The bounds the chassis' `kb_search` tool already imposes, repeated on
# the side that pays: the gateway is what turns a search into an
# embedding call, so a kb-only agent must be unable to cause embedding
# spend it could not already cause by searching. `kb_search` TRUNCATES
# an over-long query; the gateway REFUSES it, because a truncating
# gateway would silently embed something other than what was asked for.
#
# They are here rather than in `.env` because the gateway in a container
# never reads `.env` — it is handed this file, `agent-keys.env` and its
# own `environment:` block, and nothing else (decision L28). Posture
# rather than a runtime default: a spend ceiling should move by reviewed
# deployment, not by a web toggle.
# KB_EMBED_MAX_QUERIES=20
# KB_EMBED_MAX_QUERY_CHARS=1000
